### [P1] Keep both Vercel AI SDK v4 requests compatible with the selected model

**Disposition:** REQUIRED · **Severity:** IMPORTANT · **Relationship:** Introduced compatibility failure.

**Location:** `examples/example-ai-vercel-ai/anthropic.ts:28`, RIGHT; also `examples/example-ai-vercel-ai/anthropic-streaming.ts:37`.

Running either Vercel example with its locked dependencies sends **`model: "claude-sonnet-5-5"` together with `temperature: 0`**, even though the script never sets temperature. This is incompatible with the selected model's sampling contract, so the provider operation cannot produce its normal generated or streamed output. The expected request must use sampling settings supported by the selected model. No malformed inputs or unusual timing are necessary.

The [example lockfile](https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-js/blob/002a6110873a61acb7a3d77afde9b22cf34ca78a/examples/example-ai-vercel-ai/pnpm-lock.yaml#L11-L31) resolves `ai@4.3.19` and `@ai-sdk/anthropic@1.2.12`:

1. AI SDK v4 [defaults omitted temperature to `0`](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/d383c37072a91dfd0cebac13893dea044d9f88fa/packages/ai/core/prompt/prepare-call-settings.ts#L98-L102).
2. Both [`generateText`](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/d383c37072a91dfd0cebac13893dea044d9f88fa/packages/ai/core/generate-text/generate-text.ts#L407-L416) and [`streamText`](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/d383c37072a91dfd0cebac13893dea044d9f88fa/packages/ai/core/generate-text/stream-text.ts#L1040-L1049) pass the prepared settings to the provider.
3. The Anthropic adapter [includes that temperature](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/5fef22aa62c5033f418195876a34e721fffb2576/packages/anthropic/src/anthropic-messages-language-model.ts#L132-L169). Its removal branch requires explicit old-style thinking options, which these examples do not supply.
4. Locked `@ai-sdk/provider-utils@2.2.8` [serializes the body using ordinary `JSON.stringify`](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/f3487a3fac83018cb2597a13f7a1d9e24d3caa1d/packages/provider-utils/src/post-to-api.ts#L11-L40), preserving numeric zero.

The adapter uses API version `2023-06-01`. Anthropic's [API migration guide, “Sampling parameters are removed”](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/migration-2026-10-21#sampling-parameters-are-removed), distinguishes the newer API's blanket parameter removal from older-version behavior: temperature defaults to **1.0**, and Claude 4.7-and-later models already accept only defaults. Thus this specific **non-default `0` remains incompatible on the adapter's older API version**; the finding does not rely solely on newer-version parameter removal. The [Sonnet 5.5 model guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/overview#good-to-know) also directs callers away from sampling parameters. Documentation accessed November 5, 2026.

At the merge base, the same dependencies send `temperature: 0` to Sonnet 4.5, where non-default sampling is supported. Only the model changes here, making this an introduced incompatibility rather than the future retirement failure. The finding is confined to these two Vercel examples, not all PostHog AI integrations.

Consider selecting an active model compatible with these deliberately v4 examples, or making both Sonnet 5.5 requests omit unsupported sampling settings. Merely setting `temperature: undefined` does not help because v4 restores `0`. Enabling old budget-based thinking is not a suitable workaround either; Sonnet 5.5 rejects that mode. Add request-contract coverage for both generation paths.

#### Executed regression evidence

Under Node **24.13.0**, the actual pinned `prepareCallSettings`, provider `getArgs`, and tool-preparation functions were isolated and executed with equivalent inputs. Only model selection differed. Prompt conversion and absent provider-options handling were controlled stubs; neither alters sampling. A compatibility assertion checked the selected model's documented sampling restriction.

| Control | `max_tokens` | Observed temperature | Exit/result |
| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| Base model, generation configuration | 4096 | 0 | **0 — pass** |
| Head model, generation configuration | 4096 | 0 | **1 — compatibility assertion failed** |
| Base model, streaming configuration | 1024 | 0 | **0 — pass** |
| Head model, streaming configuration | 1024 | 0 | **1 — compatibility assertion failed** |

Both head failures were `AssertionError: The selected model must accept the generated sampling settings`, not import/setup failures. Commands used `request-regression.cjs base generate`, `head generate`, `base stream`, and `head stream` under the same sandbox.

**Limits:** These are executed request-building/model-configuration controls, not full checkout/public-entry runs or observed Anthropic HTTP 400 responses. No fix was applied or tested.

#### Public-entry regression sketch — NOT EXECUTED

In separately audited disposable base/head copies of the Vercel example with its exact locked dependencies, save this beside the scripts as `request-compat.test.mjs`; run **`node --test request-compat.test.mjs`**. It exercises the supported public calls and custom-fetch option without contacting Anthropic:

```js
import test from 'node:test'
import assert from 'node:assert/strict'
import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises'
import { generateText, streamText } from 'ai'
import { createAnthropic } from '@ai-sdk/anthropic'

for (const [file, streaming] of [
    ['anthropic.ts', false],
    ['anthropic-streaming.ts', true],
]) {
    test(file, { timeout: 10000 }, async () => {
        const source = await readFile(new URL(file, import.meta.url), 'utf8')
        const modelId = source.match(/model:\s*anthropic\('([^']+)'\)/)?.[1]
        assert.ok(['claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'claude-sonnet-5-5'].includes(modelId))
        const requests = []
        const provider = createAnthropic({
            apiKey: 'test-only-placeholder',
            fetch: async (_url, init) => {
                requests.push(JSON.parse(String(init.body)))
                throw new Error('Captured; network disabled')
            },
        })
        const options = {
            model: provider(modelId),
            prompt: 'Explain observability in three sentences.',
            maxRetries: 0,
        }
        try {
            if (streaming) {
                const result = streamText({ ...options, maxTokens: 1024, onError: () => {} })
                for await (const _part of result.fullStream) {}
            } else {
                await generateText(options)
            }
        } catch { /* Fetch intentionally stops completion after capture. */ }
        assert.equal(requests.length, 1, 'must reach transport')
        assert.equal(requests[0].model, modelId)
        if (modelId === 'claude-sonnet-5-5') {
            assert.ok(requests[0].temperature === undefined || requests[0].temperature === 1,
                'Sonnet 5.5 cannot use the injected non-default temperature')
        } else {
            assert.equal(requests[0].temperature, 0, 'base default control')
        }
    })
}
```

Expected but **not observed** public-entry results: both base controls pass; both head controls fail on temperature `0`.
